{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794233771,"nonce":"1WGFN6iWbEvKqXgMjS/315X0Hng=","title":"L2 — Persist writes to the same file can land out of order","message":"## Symptom\nEach persist spawns an independent `spawn_blocking` job; two jobs for the same file race, and the older snapshot can be renamed into place last. Should: the file on disk always reflects the latest issued state.\n\n## Cause\n- `src/app.rs:2047` — `blocking()` spawns per call with no ordering.\n- `src/app.rs:1941` `persist_workspace` (fires on every `SetTheme`/root change), `:1949` `persist_repos`, `:1956` `persist_issues` (fires after every write: `:1344`, `:1528`, `:1851`).\n- `src/workspace.rs:162` `atomic_write` makes each write atomic but not ordered relative to others.\n\nAlso on this path: `src/cache.rs:113` and `:125` copy the whole slice (`repos.to_vec()`, `issues.to_vec()`) just to serialize, on top of the `entry.issues.clone()` the callers already made.\n\n## Files\n- `src/app.rs:1941-1969`, `:2047` — persist helpers\n- `src/writes.rs:41` — `WriteQueue` / `Ticket`, reuse for ordering\n- `src/cache.rs:110-128` — save fns\n\n## Approach\n- Hold a second `WriteQueue` in `App` for persistence; `enter()` synchronously in each `persist_*` with a per-file key (workspace config, repos file, repo root for issues), then in the task `ticket.turn().await` before `spawn_blocking`. Issue order = disk order.\n- In `cache.rs`, serialize through borrowed structs (`ReposFileRef\u003c'a\u003e { repos: \u0026'a [RepoInfo] }`, same for issues) so `save_*` stop copying.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Unit test: two persists to the same key issued A then B, with A's job delayed, leave B on disk (follow `src/writes.rs` test style with `tokio::time`)\n- `cache.rs` save fns no longer call `to_vec()`; cache round-trip tests still pass\n- `cargo test`, clippy and fmt gates pass","files":null}]}